      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your sensation of finality suggests the well isn't just dry; your creative identity may have reached a natural conclusion that feels too heavy to dismiss as a mere phase. This profound shift from creator to observer often precedes a quiet period of maturation rather than an abrupt end to life's deeper purpose. Since forcing creation feels like lying, try treating the silence not as emptiness but as a canvas for new, non-visual expressions before deciding on your next chapter.",
      "source": "target",
